{
  "gameVersion": "2025.10",
  "dataQuality": "unverified",
  "sources": [
    "https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Buildings (CC BY-SA)"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Footprints are read from each building's wiki page and are real; `weight` is not a game stat but this project's opinion of how much an ability line is worth for crossing that building.",
    "Weights are tiered by what a defence does to an attack rather than by its damage number: Air Defense, Eagle Artillery and Spell Tower at the top because they are what an air or hero attack dies to, then the heavy splash and single-target buildings, and Mortar and Bomb Tower near the bottom because a hero walks through both. `lib/practice/scoring.ts` holds the rules layered on top.",
    "`auraRadius` is a real game number, unlike `weight`. Only the Spell Tower has one — its aura reaches well past its 2x2 footprint, so a line that comes close still counts for something.",
    "Non-square buildings are excluded; the trainer assumes square footprints.",
    "Walls are 1x1 and placed in bulk; they are a normal placeable type here.",
    "availableAt / maxLevelAt are per Town Hall level, read from each building's wiki page. Types without them (event and merged buildings) are never hidden by the Town Hall filter.",
    "Crafted defences rotate: only three exist per season and only one may stand in a village at a time. `retired: true` marks ones from past seasons — they stay in this list so existing share links keep decoding, but the trainer hides them.",
    "From TH16 the game merges pairs of defences into stronger ones and consumes the sources: 2 Cannons -> Ricochet Cannon, 2 Archer Towers -> Multi-Archer Tower, 2 Wizard Towers -> Super Wizard Tower, 1 Cannon + 1 Archer Tower -> Multi-Gear Tower. `mergedFrom` records the recipe and lib/practice/limits.ts spends the source counts, so availableAt stays the unmerged maximum it is on the wiki.",
    "`concealed` marks a building the attacker cannot see until it fires. Only the Hidden Tesla has it; the isometric board leaves those out while everything else about them is normal."
  ],
